# RNN-MD File Structure Guide

## Root Directory Files

### Core Scripts
- [RNN-MD.py](mdc:RNN-MD.py) - Main orchestration script with hyperparameter grid search
- [format.py](mdc:format.py) - Data preprocessing and formatting utility
- [model_train.py](mdc:model_train.py) - Standalone training script for single runs
- [result.py](mdc:result.py) - Results analysis and visualization generator

### Configuration & Setup
- [setup.sh](mdc:setup.sh) - Automated installation script for dependencies
- [requirements.txt](mdc:requirements.txt) - Python package dependencies
- [README.md](mdc:README.md) - Project documentation and usage instructions

### Documentation
- [code_architecture.png](mdc:code_architecture.png) - Visual workflow diagram
- [LICENCE](mdc:LICENCE) - Project license file

## Directory Structure

### RE-Net/ - Neural Network Framework
The [RE-Net/](mdc:RE-Net) directory contains the modified recurrent graph neural network implementation:

**Core Model Files:**
- [RE-Net/model.py](mdc:RE-Net/model.py) - Main RNN model architecture
- [RE-Net/RGCN.py](mdc:RE-Net/RGCN.py) - Relational Graph Convolutional Network components
- [RE-Net/Aggregator.py](mdc:RE-Net/Aggregator.py) - Graph aggregation functions
- [RE-Net/global_model.py](mdc:RE-Net/global_model.py) - Global model components

**Training Scripts:**
- [RE-Net/pretrain.py](mdc:RE-Net/pretrain.py) - Model pre-training
- [RE-Net/train.py](mdc:RE-Net/train.py) - Main training loop
- [RE-Net/test.py](mdc:RE-Net/test.py) - Model testing and evaluation

**Utilities:**
- [RE-Net/utils.py](mdc:RE-Net/utils.py) - Helper functions and data loading
- [RE-Net/data/](mdc:RE-Net/data) - Training data directory (created during runs)
- [RE-Net/baselines/](mdc:RE-Net/baselines) - Baseline comparison methods

### Runtime Directories
- `test-run/` - Example interaction data for testing
- `example-run/` - Additional example datasets
- `prerprint_output/` - Output from previous runs
- `results/` - Generated results and predictions (created during execution)

## Data Flow
1. Input data in `test-run/` or `example-run/`
2. [format.py](mdc:format.py) processes data → `RE-Net/data/<case_id>/`
3. [RE-Net/](mdc:RE-Net) scripts train models using processed data
4. [result.py](mdc:result.py) generates analysis → `results/` directory

## Important Notes
- The [RE-Net/data/](mdc:RE-Net/data) directory is dynamically created during runs
- Results are stored in timestamped directories under `results/`
- Each run generates metadata files with hyperparameter information
